# For builds whose context is the repo root: the backend image
# (docker/az acr build -f backend/Dockerfile .), which includes the agents
# package because the API runs Boardy. `az acr build` uploads the whole context
# first, so everything not needed stays out, above all secrets and
# agents/tmp/, which holds real-ish documents and must never be uploaded.
# (The agents job image builds from agents/ with agents/.dockerignore.)
#
# No trailing "/" on folder rules: `az acr build` ignores such rules when it
# packs the upload (Docker accepts both), and then uploads everything,
# frontend/node_modules and agents/tmp included.
.git
.vscode
**/.vscode
*.code-workspace
frontend
infra
tools
**/.env
**/.env.*
!**/.env.example
**/.venv
**/__pycache__
**/*.pyc
**/*.db
**/.pytest_cache
**/.mypy_cache
agents/tmp
agents/tests
agents/scripts
agents/evaluation
agents/deploy
agents/Dockerfile
agents/.dockerignore
backend/tests
backend/.dockerignore
